Functions:
1. Name: shortenURL
    Description: Shortens a given URL and returns a shortened link.
    Input: {"url": "Required. String. The URL to be shortened."}
    Output: Returns a JSON object containing the shortened URL, such as {"shortened_url": "https://gotiny.io/abc123"}

2. Name: expandURL
    Description: Expands a given shortened URL and returns the original link.
    Input: {"shortened_url": "Required. String. The shortened URL to be expanded."}
    Output: Returns a JSON object containing the original URL, such as {"original_url": "https://www.example.com"}

3. Name: customShortenURL
    Description: Shortens a given URL with a custom alias and returns a shortened link.
    Input: {"url": "Required. String. The URL to be shortened.", "alias": "Required. String. The custom alias for the shortened URL."}
    Output: Returns a JSON object containing the shortened URL with the custom alias, such as {"shortened_url": "https://gotiny.io/custom"}

4. Name: deleteShortenedURL
    Description: Deletes a given shortened URL from the system.
    Input: {"shortened_url": "Required. String. The shortened URL to be deleted."}
    Output: Returns a JSON object indicating whether the deletion was successful, such as {"success": true}

5. Name: listShortenedURLs
    Description: Lists all shortened URLs created by the user.
    Input: {"page": "Optional. Integer. The page number of the results to return. Default is 1.", "limit": "Optional. Integer. The maximum number of results to return per page. Default is 10."}
    Output: Returns a JSON object containing a list of shortened URLs created by the user, such as {"shortened_urls": [{"shortened_url": "https://gotiny.io/abc123", "original_url": "https://www.example.com"}, {"shortened_url": "https://gotiny.io/custom", "original_url": "https://www.example.com/custom"}]}

